--TEST--
a `string|tainted string` -- the shape a `?tainted string` takes the moment `??` gives it a default -- is admitted arm by arm wherever the atom would be, and the mark still decides the answer -- `rule:security/unclassified-parameter-refuses-tainted`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `Core\Env::get` answers `?tainted string`, so `?? "…"` is how an environment
// read is written and `string|tainted string` is the shape it arrives in.
// Nothing in this case is a corner: it is the only spelling that door has.
?tainted string $configured = Core\Env::get("NVS_CASE_UNSET_ORIGIN");
var $chosen = $configured ?? "host.example";

// A `Qual::Launder` parameter takes it: the arms are narrowed one at a time
// and each is admissible, so a union is admitted exactly where every arm is.
// The answer is the plain `string` the row declares -- laundering is the whole
// contract of the mark, and a union argument does not weaken it.
string $encoded = Core\Uri::encodeComponent($chosen);
echo $encoded, "\n";

// A `Qual::Neutral` parameter takes the same union, and answers plain for the
// other reason: a count carries no byte of its subject.
uint $n = Core\Str::length($chosen);
echo $n, "\n";

// A `Qual::Contagious` parameter takes it and carries the qualifier out --
// `carries_tainted` reads the tainted arm the atom question cannot see, which
// is what stops the admission above from laundering by union. The refusal that
// pins this is `a-union-carrying-tainted-still-refuses-where-the-atom-does`.
tainted bytes $decoded = Core\Uri::decodeComponent($chosen);
echo $decoded as string, "\n";

// The union is a property of the value, not of the call: with both arms plain,
// the same three calls answer exactly what they answer for a bare `string`.
var $plain = "host.example";
string $twice = Core\Uri::decodeComponent(Core\Uri::encodeComponent($plain)) as string;
echo $twice, "\n";
--EXPECT--
host.example
12
host.example
host.example
